    "body": "## Problem\n\nWith 'nottimeout' or a negative 'ttimeoutlen', a terminal response that ends with `ESC \\` is typed as keys, even when it arrives in one read. `handle_raw_buffer()` pushes input up to each ESC, and `tk_getkeys()` forces the incomplete sequence before the `ESC \\` is pushed. E.g. the OSC 11 response at startup replaces the character under the cursor with \"g\".\n\nFixes #29047\n\n## Solution\n\nUse a timeout of 0 instead, as `tinput_read_cb()` already does, so the rest of the input that was read is processed first.\n\nKeys still resolve without waiting. One difference: `<Esc>` followed by an escape sequence in the same read now combines as it does with 'ttimeout' (`ESC ESC [ A` is `<M-Up>`, was `<Esc><Up>`).\n\nAI assistance: this draft was prepared and opened by an AI agent (Claude Code) operating my account. It stays a draft until I have reviewed and tested it myself, per CONTRIBUTING.md.\n",
